## 17. Config Changes from v15

- `format_version = 4`
- Added `pointer_checksum_algo`.
- `dedup.enabled = false`
- `dedup.algo` immutable, stored in Config Snapshot.
- `[buffer].block_size` → `[buffer].granularity`.
- `[journal]` section removed.
- Superblock `journal_sequence` renamed to `wal_sequence`.
- `[mount_hints]` remains runtime-only and excluded from Config Snapshot.

## 17b. Changes from v17

- Config Snapshot confirmed as the permanent format (TOML text, Section 5) — the competing fixed-offset binary struct proposal that circulated separately is discarded.
- Restored `root_hash_algo_id` to the Superblock (Section 4).
- Restored distinct backup copies for Config Snapshot, Meta/User Table, and Function Table (Section 12) — previously only Superblock and the Parity Block had real redundancy.
- Pinned down the LBA4–5 fallback pointer field layout (Section 3.2/3.3).
- Stated the config_self_checksum algorithm (xxhash64) and a 4080-byte bound on the stripped TOML (Section 5).
- Stated the sync rule across the three `generation` fields (Section 7).
- Assigned `anchor_id` values and bounded the ANCHOR_DIFF payload size (Section 9.3).
- Clarified which block receives the WAL allocation-log entry on rollover (Section 10.1).
- Added WAL region sizing guidance using config.fs's real key names (Section 10.2b).
- Added an in-place content update protocol (Section 13.3), needed now that Section 12 has more structures with real backups to keep in sync.
- Split Recovery Order into three failure-domain tracks (Section 14).
- Split the conflated algorithm ID table into four independent tables (Section 16).

---

## 18. Known Open Gaps

Not resolved in this document — flagged rather than silently left implicit:

- **Data-block / B-tree node checksum storage layout is entirely undocumented.** `data_checksum_algo_id` selects an algorithm (Section 16), but nothing here specifies where or how that checksum is stored per data block or B-tree node, or confirms/denies the I/O engine's separate claim that xxhash64 output gets truncated to 4 bytes for storage. This needs its own design pass — the B-tree node and extent formats aren't in this document at all.
- **WAL Block Header checksum (Section 9.1) covers the header plus all current entries, recomputed on every append** — O(block_size) cost per write as the block fills. Left as-is; noting it here as an acknowledged tradeoff rather than a resolved decision, in case it wasn't the intended one.
- `config.fs [identity].uuid_sequence`, `volume_label`, `volume_label_strict` remain crash-critical fields with no protocol role described anywhere in this document. Treated as inert passthrough data carried in the Config Snapshot's TOML text; no action taken.

